# Sweet Potato, Chickpea & Spinach Curry

Based on [https://www.jamieoliver.com/recipes/…](https://www.jamieoliver.com/recipes/vegetables/sweet-potato-chickpea-amp-spinach-curry) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250729025448/https://www.jamieoliver.com/recipes/vegetables/sweet-potato-chickpea-amp-spinach-curry/))

{ rating="4" image="sweet_potato_chickpea_and_spinach_curry.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2 [red onions]{ ing="red-onions" }, finely diced
- [ ] 3 Tbsp Patak Rogan [Josh Curry Paste]{ ing="josh-curry-paste" } (or comparable Curry Paste)
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [ground ginger]{ ing="ground-ginger" } (1cm grated if fresh)
- [ ] 2 tsp of [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" } or coriander
- [ ] 2 [sweet potatoes]{ ing="sweet-potatoes" }, 2cm cubes
- [ ] 400ml (~13.5 oz) can of [chickpeas]{ ing="chickpeas" }, drained
- [ ] 400ml (~13.5 oz) can of [chopped tomatoes]{ ing="chopped-tomatoes" }
- [ ] 400ml (~13.5 oz) can of [light coconut milk]{ ing="light-coconut-milk" }
- [ ] Bag of [spinach]{ ing="spinach" }
- [ ] 2 cups [uncooked rice]{ ing="uncooked-rice" }, Naan, or other base

## Recipe

1. Prep the [onions]{ ing="red-onions" } and [sweet potatoes]{ ing="sweet-potatoes" }. Start the [rice]{ ing="uncooked-rice" }
1. Heat 2 Tbsps of oil in a large pot over medium heat
1. Saute the [onions]{ ing="red-onions" } with the [curry paste]{ ing="josh-curry-paste" }. Cook for 10m until soft and golden
1. Add the [ginger]{ ing="ground-ginger" }, coriander, sweet potato, [chickpeas]{ ing="chickpeas" }, [tomatoes]{ ing="chopped-tomatoes" }, and 200 ml water to the pan. Bring to a boil

   1. Reduce the heat to a simmer, then cover and cook for 10-15 min
1. Remove the lid, then cook for a further 15-20 min, stirring occasionally, or until the sweet potato is cooked through and the sauce thickened
1. Stir in the [coconut milk]{ ing="light-coconut-milk" } and cook for a couple of minutes, then stir in the [spinach]{ ing="spinach" } and cook until wilted

## Notes

1. You could add chopped cauliflower, red pepper, or aubergine before the sweet potato; throw in shredded cooked chicken with the tomatoes; add raw prawns or white fish pieces 5 minutes before the end of the cooking time; or serve in a flatbread with grated carrot, coriander, and shredded lettuce

### Comparison to Other Curries

- **vs [Slow Cooker Lentil Curry](../soup/slow_cooker_lentil_curry.html):** This uses curry paste shortcut vs individual ground spices; light coconut milk vs no coconut (tahini/yogurt finish); chickpeas/sweet potato vs lentils/peas; stovetop quick (30 min) vs slow cooker (7.5 hrs)
- **Recipe philosophy:** Practical curry paste approach for weeknight cooking while maintaining complex flavor; light coconut milk keeps it from being overpowering
